2026-09-11 21:57 UTC-0300 Itamar Lins  <itamarlins at gmail.com>
  ### Fixed
   - source/common/procmisc/cfuncs.c EDI_UTF8_LOWER, EDI_UTF8_UPPER: missing `return` after
     the error branch caused a fall-through to `hb_retclen( szDst, iDstLen )`
     with `szDst == NULL` and `iDstLen == 0`, overwriting the intended
     return value with an empty result on any conversion failure.
  ### Changed
   -  source/common/procmisc/cfuncs.c changeutf8case: switched from `malloc`/`realloc`/`free` to
     `hb_xgrab`/`hb_xrealloc`/`hb_xfree`. Required so the returned buffer
      can be handed to `hb_retclen_buffer()` without an extra copy.
   - cfuncs/EDI_UTF8_LOWER, cfuncs/EDI_UTF8_UPPER: return via
     `hb_retclen_buffer()` instead of `hb_retclen()` + `free()`. Removes
     one allocation and one copy per call.
   - cfuncs/EDI_UTF8_LOWER, cfuncs/EDI_UTF8_UPPER: store the result of
     `hb_parclen()` in `HB_SIZE` instead of `int`, avoiding truncation on
     large inputs and signed/unsigned mismatch warnings on strict builds.
   - cfuncs/EDI_UTF8_LOWER, cfuncs/EDI_UTF8_UPPER: added explicit
     `HB_ISCHAR(1)` guard with early return, so `hb_parc(1)` is never
     called on a non-string parameter.
  ### Notes
   - No `#ifdef` added. Harbour strings are byte strings in both ANSI and
     UNICODE builds; `changeutf8case` performs case folding entirely on
     UTF-8 byte sequences, so no wide-char branch is required. Verified on
     Linux GCC/Clang (32/64) and Windows MSVC, Clang-cl and MinGW-GCC
     (32/64).
  ### Fixed
  - source/common/procmisc/cfuncs.c HWG_STRREV: input longer than 511 bytes was silently truncated
    because the reversal ran against a fixed `char puffer[512]`. Now uses
    `hb_parclen()` + `hb_xgrab()` and returns the exact-length result via
    `hb_retclen_buffer()`, with no upper bound other than available memory.
  ### Changed
  - source/common/procmisc/cfuncs.c HWG_STRREV: replaced `strncpy` with `memcpy` + explicit
    null-termination. Eliminates GCC `-Wstringop-truncation` and MSVC
    `C4996` warnings and correctly preserves embedded NUL bytes.
  - HWG_STRREV: replaced the ternary fallback with an explicit
    `HB_ISCHAR(1)` guard and early return, for consistency with the rest
    of the file.
  - HWG_STRREV: `hb_retclen_buffer()` transfers buffer ownership
    to Harbour, removing the extra copy previously done by `hb_retc()`.
  ### Notes
  - No `#ifdef` added. Harbour strings are byte strings in both ANSI and
    UNICODE builds, and `reverse_string()` is already UTF-8-aware, so no
    wide-char branch is required. Verified on Linux GCC/Clang (32/64) and
    Windows MSVC, Clang-cl and MinGW-GCC (32/64).
  ### Fixed
  - source/common/procmisc/cfuncs.c HWG_CHDIR: return value was inverted. `chdir()`/`_chdir()`
    return 0 on success and -1 on failure, but the code returned the
    raw result inside a `&&` expression, so the Harbour-side value was
    `.F.` on success and `.T.` on failure. Now compares explicitly:
    `chdir(...) == 0`.
  - cfuncs/HWG_CHDIR, cfuncsL/HWG_CHDIR: used `hb_parc()` (raw UTF-8
    bytes) as the path argument. On Windows this bypasses the ANSI
    codepage conversion and on POSIX it bypasses the locale conversion,
    breaking non-ASCII paths (`João`, `Área de Trabalho`, `Café`, ...).
    Now uses `hb_parcx()` on Windows ANSI and `hb_parc()` on POSIX
    (native UTF-8).
  - cfuncs/HWG_CHDIR, cfuncsL/HWG_CHDIR: added a native UNICODE branch
    so the call is consistent under `-DUNICODE` builds and the CRT
    working-directory state is updated along with the kernel one. The
    UTF-8 -> UTF-16 conversion is done with `MultiByteToWideChar(CP_UTF8,
    ...)` + `hb_xgrab`/`hb_xfree`, since Harbour has no `hb_parcw()`.
    The path is then passed to `_wchdir()` (not `SetCurrentDirectoryW`,
    which updates only the kernel state and would leave the CRT's
    relative-path resolution out of sync).
  ### Changed
  - cfuncs/HWG_CHDIR: explicit `HB_ISCHAR(1)` guard with early
    `hb_retl( HB_FALSE )` instead of relying on `&&` short-circuit.
  - cfuncs includes: `<direct.h>` was only included under `_MSC_VER`,
    so MinGW, Clang-cl and Clang/MSYS2 builds failed with
    `call to undeclared function '_wchdir'`. Now included for every
    Windows toolchain via
    `#if defined( _WIN32 ) || defined( __WIN32__ ) || defined( __MINGW32__ )`

