2026-09-08 21:12 UTC-0300 Itamar Lins  <itamarlins at gmail.com>
  ### Fixed
  - **hcomboex.prg**: fixed 64-bit pointer truncation in the embedded C
    section - HB_FUNC(COPYDATA) read the WM_GETTEXT buffer address
    (lParam) via hb_parnl() (32-bit LONG), corrupting it on 64-bit builds
    and making lstrcpyn() write to the wrong memory; now uses
    hb_parnint(). ComboSubclassProc() still truncated wParam via
    hb_vmPushLong((LONG)wParam) - a leftover from an earlier partial fix
    that already switched lParam to HB_PUSHITEM() but missed wParam - and
    never checked HB_ISPOINTER() on the .prg's return value, so a real
    handle (e.g. the HBRUSH a combo box's WM_CTLCOLOREDIT/
    WM_CTLCOLORLISTBOX handler must return) would get truncated through
    hb_parnl(). Both now match the already-correct pattern used in
    s_MainWndProc (window.c).

