2026-08-25 22:01 UTC-0300 Itamar Lins  <itamarlins at gmail.com>
  ### Fixed source\winapi\hriched.prg
  - **hriched.prg / HRichEdit:ReadOnly**: fixed the method missing the
    `CLASS HRichEdit` clause present on every other out-of-body method in
    the file - without it the implementation wasn't bound to the
    `METHOD ReadOnly(...) SETGET` slot declared in the class body, breaking
    `::ReadOnly` / `::ReadOnly := ...` (and risking a build failure or a
    silent fallback to an unrelated global function).
  - **hriched.prg / HRichEdit:onEvent (WM_MOUSEWHEEL)**: fixed a duplicated
    `hwg_Sendmessage(EM_SCROLL, ...)` call that scrolled the control twice
    as far as intended on every mouse wheel notch.
  - **hriched.prg / HRichEdit:onEvent (ESC / WM_KEYDOWN)**: fixed
    `hwg_Getparent(...) != Nil`, which would not detect a "no parent"
    result of `0`, potentially sending `WM_CLOSE` to an invalid window
    handle. Changed to `!Empty(...)`, which safely covers both `NIL` and
    `0` without changing the already-working case.
  - **hriched.prg / HRichEdit:onEvent (WM_MOUSEWHEEL)**: fixed an off-by-one
    in the unsigned-to-signed 16-bit delta conversion
    (`> 32768 ? -65535` -> `>= 32768 ? -65536`, standard two's-complement
    conversion). No observable behavior change today (only the sign is
    used, and real wheel deltas are multiples of 120), but the formula was
    incorrect at both the boundary and the converted value.
  ### Changed
  - **hriched.prg / HRichEdit:onEvent**: documented the `::bOther` contract
    (must return a Number <= -1 to continue with default processing) with
    an inline comment, since any other return value silently short-circuits
    all default key/focus/selection handling below it.

