2026-08-25 21:07 UTC-0300 Itamar Lins  <itamarlins at gmail.com>
  ### Fixed
  - **hdrawn.prg / HDrawn:SetState (STATE_UNPRESS)**: fixed a phantom-object
    bug where `HDrawn():GetByState(...)` implicitly constructed a throwaway
    `HDrawn` instance via `New()`, whose constructor has the side effect of
    permanently registering a blank, position-less object into the shared
    default board's `aDrawn` list on every button-release event. That
    phantom (with `nLeft`/`nTop`/`nWidth`/`nHeight` all `NIL`) was then hit
    by `GetByPos()` on the very next mouse move, causing an unhandled
    `Number >= NIL` runtime error - fatal and silent in `/gui` builds.
    Replaced with `::GetByState(...)`, reusing the existing, already
    registered `Self` (the method never touches its own instance fields).
  - **hdrawn.prg / HDrawnTT:Paint**: fixed multi-line tooltips drawing the
    full, still-joined `::title` string on every line iteration instead of
    the current line (`arr[i]`), causing overlapping/duplicated text.
  - **hdrawn.prg / HDrawnRadio:SetGroupValue**: fixed `o := aDrawn[i]:xValue`
    capturing the logical value instead of the object reference; later code
    uses `o` as an object (`o:xValue`, `o:title`, `o:Refresh()`), causing an
    unhandled runtime error when `SetGroupValue()` is called with an index
    beyond the radio group's actual member count.
  - **hdrawn.prg / HDrawn:Paint (children loop)**: fixed a skipped sibling
    repaint when a child's `Paint()` removes itself from `::aDrawn` mid-loop
    (e.g. `HDrawnTT` self-deleting on hide) - the fixed-bound `FOR` loop
    didn't account for the array shrinking and shifting. Replaced with a
    `DO WHILE` that re-checks the array length after each child paint and
    only advances when nothing was removed; no extra allocation, same
    front-to-back paint order (z-order unchanged).

  ### Changed
  - **hdrawn.prg / HDrawnArrow:ArrowTimerProc**: added a defensive `NIL`
    guard for `o:oTimer`, covering a race where a queued `WM_TIMER` message
    can still fire after `onButtonUp()`/`onMouseMove()` already called
    `oTimer:End()` and set `oTimer := NIL`.

